# 22. TERMINATION AND REINSTATEMENT

**22.1.** The license remains effective for the period specified in MY IPL, subject to the duration of the licensed rights and termination under this Section.

**22.2.** If a Licensee materially breaches TCSL or MY IPL, the Licensor may provide written notice identifying the breach and requesting correction.

**22.3.** Unless a longer period is required by law or specified in the notice, the Licensee has thirty (30) calendar days from receipt of the notice to correct the breach.

**22.4.** If the breach is not corrected within the applicable correction period, the Licensor may terminate the affected license.

**22.5.** The Licensor may suspend or terminate permissions more rapidly where immediate action is reasonably necessary to address serious infringement, unlawful activity, security risks, or substantial harm, subject to Applicable Law.

**22.6.** If the breach is corrected within the applicable period, the license remains effective, unless termination has already become effective under Applicable Law.

**22.7.** Where termination has already taken effect, the Licensor may reinstate the license after the breach has been corrected and reasonable restoration conditions have been satisfied.

**22.8.** Following termination, the Licensee must stop exercising the terminated permissions and must stop further unauthorized distribution.

**22.9.** Termination does not automatically invalidate permissions previously and validly granted to compliant downstream recipients, unless Applicable Law or the terms governing those recipients provide otherwise.

**22.10.** Accrued payment obligations, ownership terms, attribution obligations, confidentiality duties, liability provisions, and other provisions that must survive by their nature remain effective to the extent permitted by law.

**22.11.** Termination does not remove any legal rights or remedies that arose before termination.

---

# 23. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION

**23.1.** TCSL is governed by the law of the jurisdiction identified in the official TCSL publication notice.

**23.2.** The selected law applies subject to mandatory rules that cannot legally be excluded or displaced.

**23.3.** The parties should first attempt to resolve disputes through good-faith communication and negotiation.

**23.4.** If negotiation does not resolve the dispute within a reasonable period, the parties may mutually agree to mediation or another lawful dispute-resolution procedure.

**23.5.** If the dispute remains unresolved, the parties may pursue the remedies and procedures available before a competent court or other competent authority under Applicable Law.

**23.6.** Nothing in this Section removes mandatory consumer, jurisdictional, or procedural rights.

**23.7.** The Governing Law field must be completed before TCSL is released as an official public licensing document.

---

# 24. VERSIONING AND UPDATES

**24.1.** Each official TCSL release must have a clearly identified version number.

**24.2.** A Product released under a particular TCSL version remains governed by that version unless a valid migration or replacement agreement is made.

**24.3.** Publication of a later TCSL version does not automatically modify the license governing a previously released Product.

**24.4.** A Rights Holder may adopt a later version for a Product through a clearly documented process and with any agreement required by Applicable Law or the existing license.

**24.5.** A Licensee must be able to identify the TCSL version and MY IPL version applicable to the Product.

**24.6.** The TCSL Publisher is responsible for identifying official releases and publishing the corresponding version information.

**24.7.** A revised document must not be represented as an official version unless it has been published or authorized by the TCSL Publisher.

---

# 25. ADOPTION OF THE TCSL FRAMEWORK

**25.1.** TecnoCore Software grants a non-exclusive, royalty-free permission to reproduce and use the unmodified official TCSL text for the purpose of licensing Products under this framework.

**25.2.** A company, developer, organization, or other rights holder may adopt TCSL if it has the authority to license the Product identified in its MY IPL.

**25.3.** An adopting Licensor must identify itself as the responsible Product Licensor in MY IPL.

**25.4.** Adoption of TCSL does not make TecnoCore Software the owner, publisher, maintainer, guarantor, or commercial representative of an independent adopter's Product.

**25.5.** The official TCSL text must not be modified and then represented as the unmodified official TCSL version.

**25.6.** An adopter may create Product-specific terms in MY IPL only within the limits established by TCSL.

**25.7.** A modified or forked licensing framework must not be presented as the official TCSL 1.0 text without authorization from the TCSL Publisher.

**25.8.** Use of TCSL does not grant permission to use TecnoCore Software trademarks, logos, or other brand assets.

**25.9.** Adoption of the framework does not imply that TecnoCore Software has reviewed, certified, endorsed, or approved the adopter's Product.

---

# 26. GENERAL PROVISIONS

**26.1. Severability:** If a provision is found invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to apply to the extent permitted by Applicable Law.

**26.2. No Waiver:** Failure to enforce a provision does not constitute a permanent waiver of that provision.

**26.3. Entire Licensing Terms:** TCSL and the applicable MY IPL constitute the licensing terms for the Product, together with any separate written agreement expressly incorporated by reference.

**26.4. Amendments:** Amendments to the terms governing an existing Product must follow Section 24 and Applicable Law.

**26.5. Notices:** Formal notices must be delivered through the contact method identified in MY IPL or the applicable official publication.

**26.6. No Employment or Partnership:** TCSL does not create an employment relationship, partnership, joint venture, agency, or representative relationship between the TCSL Publisher, Licensor, and Licensee.

**26.7. Independent Parties:** Each independent adopter remains responsible for its own Products, rights, representations, and licensing activity.

**26.8. Mandatory Law:** Nothing in TCSL excludes, limits, or waives a right or obligation that cannot legally be excluded, limited, or waived.

**26.9. Language:** The official English text is the controlling version of TCSL unless Applicable Law requires otherwise or an officially designated controlling translation is published.

**26.10. Interpretation:** Headings are provided for convenience and do not independently change the meaning of the provisions.

